  "id": "electric-potential",
  "term": "electric potential",
  "definition": "In this source, electric potential refers to the electrical state across a neuron’s membrane, including resting and action-potential conditions. It is shaped by dissolved charges in surrounding fluid and fixed charges on membrane-related structures, and its pattern can differ between healthy and pathological neurons.",
